# `run` writes the counter and `bump` reads that back and writes the next: what `bump` finds is what `run` left, so the
# route changes nothing it found. The counter stands between the step that writes it and the one that reads and uses it.

route bumped.run
step run/bump
line entry > run call
line run > File(data/counter.txt) own
line File(data/counter.txt) > run/bump own
line run/bump > File(data/counter.txt) own

side entry left
side File(data/counter.txt) between
